<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "Arcade sessions can appear as rich cards, while P2P requests use the PM header controls and leave a plain P2P line in the transcript."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_p2p}>{dgettext("help_features", "What Session Summaries Show")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "Session summaries name who created the session and walk through its lifecycle on a small timeline: when it was created, when it connected, and — once it is over — when it ended, how long it ran, and why it closed."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_btn_join}>{dgettext("help_features", "Live vs. Finished")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "While an Arcade session is still live the card can offer Join or Open. P2P Start, Join and Decline actions live in the PM header instead; finished P2P history shows final state only."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_document_alert}>{dgettext("help_features", "Notes")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "If a legacy P2P invite line can no longer find its session, it stays as inert history instead of showing stale action buttons."
  )}
</p>
